    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0326" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15237: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-21T16:00:00+07:00">January 21, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>137. Naval Attaché informed us Soong had indicated to him that his personal
                    situation was improving and there are stories current that efforts are being
                    made by one of Soong’s sisters to resolve the difficulties.</p>
                <p>Department’s 85, January 17. There are also stories, reportedly from highly
                    placed and intimately informed source, that Wei Taoming<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d261-f1"/> is to be Foreign Minister. General impression is that,
                    while there has been some improvement in Soong’s relationship with Chiang and
                    perhaps with Kung,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d261-f2"/> question of Soong’s
                    retention of Foreign Office portfolio and return to Washington in capacity of
                    Foreign Minister has not been settled. That situation is still obscure is also
                    indicated by Soong’s continued inactivity as Foreign Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
